- **Environment variable overrides:** The scripts honor two undeclared overrides that are not shown in the plugin config table:
- - `OG_CORE_URL` — changes the assessment/registration endpoint (default: `https://www.openguardrails.com/core`)
- - `OG_AGENT_NAME` — changes the agent display name sent to the platform
- If either variable is set in your shell environment, it will silently take effect. Verify they are not set, or that they point to a trusted destination, before running `activate.mjs`.
- > **Security classification: Suspicious.** Security scanners classify this skill as suspicious due to a control plane vulnerability: the `OG_CORE_URL` environment variable can silently redirect all registration and behavioral assessment traffic to an arbitrary, untrusted endpoint. The SKILL.md and `references/details.md` transparently disclose this risk, but the mechanism itself remains exploitable if an attacker gains control over the agent's environment — this is not proof of intentional malicious behavior by the skill, but it is a real attack surface.
- This package implements the advertised local guard plus an optional cloud activation, but the registry metadata omits two environment overrides (`OG_CORE_URL`, `OG_AGENT_NAME`) and the credential file path. Audit the code and provenance before activating the cloud component.
- Run `npm pack @openguardrails/moltguard`, extract the tarball, and diff `package/` against a fresh clone of the GitHub repository. Only proceed if the contents match the source you trust.
- **3. Check for undeclared environment overrides.**
- Ensure your environment does not set `OG_CORE_URL` or `OG_AGENT_NAME`, or set `OG_CORE_URL` only to the official endpoint if you trust it:
- echo $OG_CORE_URL    # must be empty or https://www.openguardrails.com/core
- echo $OG_AGENT_NAME  # inspect if set
- These variables are honored by the scripts but are not declared in the registry metadata. A malicious or accidental value for `OG_CORE_URL` will silently redirect registration and all assessment traffic.
- **4. Monitor network traffic during activation.**
- If you plan to activate the cloud component, run `tcpdump`, `mitmproxy`, or Little Snitch during registration to confirm the destination and that only sanitized metadata — not message content — is sent.
- **5. Know how to clean up credentials.**
- > **If you cannot or will not audit the package provenance and code, avoid running the activation step.** Local protections work entirely without activation — no outbound calls, no credentials written, no trust required.
- **Environment variable overrides** (scripts only, not plugin config):
- | Variable | Overrides | Description |
- |----------|-----------|-------------|
- | `OG_CORE_URL` | `coreUrl` | Registration/assessment endpoint |
- | `OG_AGENT_NAME` | `agentName` | Agent display name sent to platform |
